# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use modern tools to implement methods for error suppression, mitigation, and correction. We focus on the directed execution model using Samplomatic and addons."
msgstr "Usa herramientas modernas para implementar métodos de supresión, mitigación y corrección de errores. Nos centramos en el modelo de ejecución dirigida mediante Samplomatic y addons."

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Modern workflows"
msgstr "Workflows modernos"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Modern workflows {#modern-workflows}"
msgstr "Workflows modernos {#modern-workflows}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This course has covered a wide variety of methods for handling quantum noise and errors. We intentionally avoided some black-box solutions so that we could see how these methods work. Now we are ready to use these methods in their most modern form. Specifically, we explore some highly optimized error-handling tools that hide some of the complexity from us. We also explore Samplomatic and addons such as shaded lightcones (SLC), which give us very fine control over certain mitigation processes.\n"
msgstr "Este curso ha cubierto una amplia variedad de métodos para manejar el ruido y los errores cuánticos. Evitamos intencionadamente algunas soluciones de caja negra para poder ver cómo funcionan estos métodos. Ahora estamos listos para usar estos métodos en su forma más moderna. En concreto, exploramos algunas herramientas de manejo de errores altamente optimizadas que nos ocultan parte de la complejidad. También exploramos Samplomatic y addons como los shaded lightcones (SLC), que nos dan un control muy fino sobre ciertos procesos de mitigación.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this video, Dr. Chris Porter gives an overview of these modern tools. We plan to add example workflows to this lesson at a later date. However, this lesson already contains all the information that you need to use these tools and to pass the badging exam.\n"
msgstr "En este video, el Dr. Chris Porter ofrece una visión general de estas herramientas modernas. Planeamos añadir workflows de ejemplo a esta lección más adelante. Sin embargo, esta lección ya contiene toda la información que necesitas para usar estas herramientas y aprobar el examen de insignia.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<IBMVideo id=\"135107080\" title=\"In this video, Chris Porter provides an overview of modern tools for handling errors in quantum computation.\"/>\n"
msgstr "<IBMVideo id=\"135107080\" title=\"En este video, Chris Porter ofrece una visión general de las herramientas modernas para manejar errores en la computación cuántica.\"/>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overview {#overview}"
msgstr "Visión general {#overview}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Early IBM Quantum primitives, such as Estimator and Sampler, exposed error mitigation through a small number of preset levels. Later releases provided more direct control over individual techniques, including choices of zero-noise extrapolation strategy, Pauli twirling configurations, and randomization parameters. However, these settings remained largely global, and applied uniformly across an entire circuit.\n"
msgstr "Las primeras primitivas de IBM Quantum, como Estimator y Sampler, exponían la mitigación de errores mediante un pequeño número de niveles predefinidos. Versiones posteriores ofrecieron un control más directo sobre técnicas individuales, incluidas las opciones de estrategia de extrapolación a ruido cero, las configuraciones de Pauli twirling y los parámetros de aleatorización. Sin embargo, estos ajustes seguían siendo en gran medida globales y se aplicaban de manera uniforme a todo un circuito.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A diagram showing that different phases of execution models have increased user control.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/phases.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A diagram showing that different phases of execution models have increased user control.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/phases.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As quantum workloads become more sophisticated, developers increasingly need the ability to tailor execution and mitigation strategies to specific regions of a circuit. The following diagram outlines several key tools that this lesson discusses, and shows where they fit within a typical workflow.\n"
msgstr "A medida que las cargas de trabajo cuánticas se vuelven más sofisticadas, los desarrolladores necesitan cada vez más la capacidad de adaptar las estrategias de ejecución y mitigación a regiones específicas de un circuito. El siguiente diagrama describe varias herramientas clave que se tratan en esta lección y muestra dónde encajan dentro de un workflow típico.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A diagram showing that workflows typically progress from mapping problems to quantum circuits, to transpilation and optimization, to execution and post-processing. Each of these steps has modern tools associated with it.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/workflow.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A diagram showing that workflows typically progress from mapping problems to quantum circuits, to transpilation and optimization, to execution and post-processing. Each of these steps has modern tools associated with it.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/workflow.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The directed execution model addresses the need for modular control over execution, and it integrates many of these tools.\n"
msgstr "El modelo de ejecución dirigida responde a la necesidad de un control modular sobre la ejecución e integra muchas de estas herramientas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Directed execution model {#directed-execution-model}"
msgstr "Modelo de ejecución dirigida {#directed-execution-model}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rather than making implicit execution decisions, the directed execution model follows user-provided directives. This approach improves transparency and makes complex workflows easier to inspect and debug. Some key features of this model include:\n"
msgstr "En lugar de tomar decisiones de ejecución implícitas, el modelo de ejecución dirigida sigue directivas proporcionadas por el usuario. Este enfoque mejora la transparencia y facilita la inspección y la depuración de workflows complejos. Algunas características clave de este modelo son:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Per-layer configuration through labeled circuit regions\n"
msgstr "Configuración por capa mediante regiones de circuito etiquetadas\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Identification of unique and repeated layers for efficient noise learning\n"
msgstr "Identificación de capas únicas y repetidas para un aprendizaje de ruido eficiente\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Batched execution workflows\n"
msgstr "Workflows de ejecución por lotes\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Structured post-processing\n"
msgstr "Posprocesamiento estructurado\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Close integration with addons such as shaded lightcones\n"
msgstr "Estrecha integración con addons como los shaded lightcones\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The model is built around two key components:\n"
msgstr "El modelo se construye en torno a dos componentes clave:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Samplomatic, which defines execution recipes\n"
msgstr "Samplomatic, que define recetas de ejecución\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Executor, which carries out those recipes and returns samples\n"
msgstr "Executor, que lleva a cabo esas recetas y devuelve muestras\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Most workflows that use Executor can also be implemented with Sampler, because both ultimately produce samples. The key advantage of Executor is efficiency. Tasks such as generating twirling configurations are often much faster in the server-side near-time environment than on the client. Estimator and Sampler remain supported, and might still be the most convenient choice for many workloads.\n"
msgstr "La mayoría de los workflows que usan Executor también pueden implementarse con Sampler, porque ambos producen muestras en última instancia. La ventaja clave de Executor es la eficiencia. Tareas como generar configuraciones de twirling suelen ser mucho más rápidas en el entorno de casi tiempo real del lado del servidor que en el cliente. Estimator y Sampler siguen siendo compatibles y podrían seguir siendo la opción más conveniente para muchas cargas de trabajo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before execution, however, you must construct and prepare a circuit. Qiskit provides several addons that help with circuit generation, simulation, and optimization. For more information about any of the following tools, follow the links.\n"
msgstr "Sin embargo, antes de la ejecución debes construir y preparar un circuito. Qiskit ofrece varios addons que ayudan con la generación, simulación y optimización de circuitos. Para obtener más información sobre cualquiera de las siguientes herramientas, sigue los enlaces.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build quantum circuits {#build-quantum-circuits}"
msgstr "Construir circuitos cuánticos {#build-quantum-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For some applications or new approaches, users must determine how to map their problem to a quantum circuit. In many domains, however, Qiskit addons can automate important parts of this process.\n"
msgstr "Para algunas aplicaciones o enfoques nuevos, los usuarios deben determinar cómo asignar su problema a un circuito cuántico. Sin embargo, en muchos dominios, los addons de Qiskit pueden automatizar partes importantes de este proceso.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Optimization mapper {#optimization-mapper}"
msgstr "Optimization mapper {#optimization-mapper}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Optimization mapper](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-opt-mapper) helps express classical optimization problems in forms that are suitable for quantum algorithms. Key functionality includes:\n"
msgstr "[Optimization mapper](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-opt-mapper) ayuda a expresar problemas de optimización clásicos en formas adecuadas para algoritmos cuánticos. Su funcionalidad clave incluye:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Construct objective functions and constraints\n"
msgstr "Construir funciones objetivo y restricciones\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Convert problems into QUBO formulations\n"
msgstr "Convertir problemas en formulaciones QUBO\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generate Hamiltonian or operator representations\n"
msgstr "Generar representaciones de hamiltoniano u operador\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![An image of a molecule and graph being mapped to qubits.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/mappers.avif)\n"
msgstr "![An image of a molecule and graph being mapped to qubits.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/mappers.avif)\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fermionic mapper {#fermionic-mapper}"
msgstr "Fermionic mapper {#fermionic-mapper}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Fermionic mapper](/addons/qiskit-fermions) converts fermionic operators into qubit operators that are suitable for quantum hardware. It supports mappings such as Jordan-Wigner, which converts operators on indistinguishable fermions to Pauli operators on distinguishable qubits, while preserving fermionic statistics. This addon is useful for quantum chemistry and materials science applications.\n"
msgstr "[Fermionic mapper](/addons/qiskit-fermions) convierte operadores fermiónicos en operadores de qubits adecuados para hardware cuántico. Admite mapeos como Jordan-Wigner, que convierte operadores sobre fermiones indistinguibles en operadores de Pauli sobre qubits distinguibles, preservando al mismo tiempo la estadística fermiónica. Este addon es útil para aplicaciones de química cuántica y ciencia de materiales.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The previous two addons focus on the initial mapping of a problem structure to a quantum circuit. It is equally important, however, to efficiently map the time evolution of a process onto a quantum circuit, and to optimize a circuit by reducing its depth. The next few addons address these tasks.\n"
msgstr "Los dos addons anteriores se centran en el mapeo inicial de la estructura de un problema a un circuito cuántico. Sin embargo, es igualmente importante asignar de manera eficiente la evolución temporal de un proceso a un circuito cuántico y optimizar un circuito reduciendo su profundidad. Los siguientes addons abordan estas tareas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Multi-product formulas (MPF) {#multi-product-formulas-mpf}"
msgstr "Fórmulas multiproducto (MPF) {#multi-product-formulas-mpf}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Multi-product formulas](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-mpf) improve the accuracy of quantum time-evolution simulations by combining multiple approximations. Specifically, you create circuits with varying numbers of Trotter steps, so that you can use a weighted combination of the circuit results. For a given target accuracy, MPF can often use shallower circuits than standard Trotter methods. The cost is that you must run multiple circuits and combine their results classically.\n"
msgstr "[Las fórmulas multiproducto](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-mpf) mejoran la precisión de las simulaciones de evolución temporal cuántica combinando múltiples aproximaciones. En concreto, creas circuitos con distintos números de pasos de Trotter, de modo que puedas usar una combinación ponderada de los resultados de los circuitos. Para una precisión objetivo dada, MPF a menudo puede usar circuitos menos profundos que los métodos de Trotter estándar. El costo es que debes ejecutar varios circuitos y combinar sus resultados de forma clásica.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![An image showing Trotter circuits with different numbers of steps.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/mpf.avif)\n"
msgstr "![An image showing Trotter circuits with different numbers of steps.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/mpf.avif)\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "AQC-Tensor {#aqc-tensor}"
msgstr "AQC-Tensor {#aqc-tensor}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[AQC-Tensor](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-aqc-tensor) performs approximate quantum compilation using tensor-network methods. A common use case is to replace a portion of a deep circuit with a shallower variational approximation. The resulting circuit can achieve similar accuracy with significantly less depth.\n"
msgstr "[AQC-Tensor](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-aqc-tensor) realiza compilación cuántica aproximada mediante métodos de redes tensoriales. Un caso de uso común es reemplazar una parte de un circuito profundo por una aproximación variacional menos profunda. El circuito resultante puede alcanzar una precisión similar con una profundidad significativamente menor.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![An image showing the first few layers of a quantum circuit being compressed using AQC.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/aqc.avif)\n"
msgstr "![An image showing the first few layers of a quantum circuit being compressed using AQC.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/aqc.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpilation {#transpilation}"
msgstr "Transpilación {#transpilation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You have already used transpilation many times in this course. You know that after an abstract circuit is constructed, it must be prepared for execution on hardware. However, we have not yet explored the multiple stages of transpilation in detail.\n"
msgstr "Ya has usado la transpilación muchas veces en este curso. Sabes que, una vez construido un circuito abstracto, debe prepararse para su ejecución en hardware. Sin embargo, aún no hemos explorado en detalle las múltiples etapas de la transpilación.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Key transpilation stages include:\n"
msgstr "Las etapas clave de la transpilación incluyen:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Layout: map logical qubits to physical qubits\n"
msgstr "Layout: asignar qubits lógicos a qubits físicos\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Translation: rewrite operations using the backend's native gate set\n"
msgstr "Traducción: reescribir las operaciones usando el conjunto de puertas nativas del backend\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Routing: insert and optimize SWAP operations required by hardware connectivity\n"
msgstr "Enrutamiento: insertar y optimizar las operaciones SWAP requeridas por la conectividad del hardware\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These processes are interrelated. For example, the layout should minimize depth even after routing is taken into account. The layout should also avoid the most error-prone qubits and connections. These stages are often automated, but advanced users might choose to specify custom layouts or other constraints when needed.\n"
msgstr "Estos procesos están interrelacionados. Por ejemplo, el layout debe minimizar la profundidad incluso después de tener en cuenta el enrutamiento. El layout también debe evitar los qubits y las conexiones más propensos a errores. Estas etapas suelen estar automatizadas, pero los usuarios avanzados pueden optar por especificar layouts personalizados u otras restricciones cuando sea necesario.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![An image showing how the qubits in an abstract quantum circuit need to be assigned to real physical qubits on a quantum computer as part of transpilation.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/transp-mapping.avif)\n"
msgstr "![An image showing how the qubits in an abstract quantum circuit need to be assigned to real physical qubits on a quantum computer as part of transpilation.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/transp-mapping.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To learn more about transpilation, see the [Introduction to transpilation](/guides/transpile) guide.\n"
msgstr "Para obtener más información sobre la transpilación, consulta la guía [Introducción a la transpilación](/guides/transpile).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding}"
msgstr "Comprueba tu comprensión {#check-your-understanding}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Look at the following quantum circuit, and assume that you need to run it on a quantum computer with a heavy-hex layout, part of which is shown. (a) Propose a mapping from the qubit numbers in the abstract circuit to the qubit numbers in the physical quantum computer that minimizes the number of SWAP gates required. (b) Is your choice unique, or might there be other equally good choices? (c) Even if your choice is the sole optimal layout for reducing SWAP gates, what are some reasons that the transpiler might choose a different mapping?\n"
msgstr "Observa el siguiente circuito cuántico y supón que necesitas ejecutarlo en una computadora cuántica con un layout heavy-hex, del que se muestra una parte. (a) Propón una asignación de los números de qubit del circuito abstracto a los números de qubit de la computadora cuántica física que minimice el número de puertas SWAP necesarias. (b) ¿Es tu elección única o podría haber otras opciones igualmente buenas? (c) Aunque tu elección sea el único layout óptimo para reducir las puertas SWAP, ¿cuáles son algunas razones por las que el transpilador podría elegir una asignación distinta?\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A two-part image. The right shows a quantum circuit with six qubits and five CNOT gates. The left shows the heavy-hex topology of a region of a real quantum computer.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/check-in-transp.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A two-part image. The right shows a quantum circuit with six qubits and five CNOT gates. The left shows the heavy-hex topology of a region of a real quantum computer.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/check-in-transp.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Answer\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Respuesta\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(a) There could be many correct answers, but note that only abstract qubit 0 has entangling (two-qubit) gates with three neighbors. All others participate in two-qubit operations with only two neighbors. This circuit can be mapped to a heavy-hex topology without any SWAP gates. Any layout that achieves this is acceptable. Using $\\text{aq[0]}$ to refer to abstract qubit zero, and $\\text{tq[0]}$ for transpiled qubit zero, one such layout is:\n"
msgstr "(a) Podría haber muchas respuestas correctas, pero ten en cuenta que solo el qubit abstracto 0 tiene puertas de entrelazamiento (de dos qubits) con tres vecinos. Todos los demás participan en operaciones de dos qubits con solo dos vecinos. Este circuito puede asignarse a una topología heavy-hex sin ninguna puerta SWAP. Cualquier layout que lo logre es aceptable. Usando $\\text{aq[0]}$ para referirnos al qubit abstracto cero, y $\\text{tq[0]}$ para el qubit transpilado cero, un layout de este tipo es:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\text{aq[0]} & \\rightarrow \\text{tq[15],}\\\\\n"
"\\text{aq[1]} & \\rightarrow \\text{tq[16],}\\\\\n"
"\\text{aq[2]} & \\rightarrow \\text{tq[19],}\\\\\n"
"\\text{aq[3]} & \\rightarrow \\text{tq[14],}\\\\\n"
"\\text{aq[4]} & \\rightarrow \\text{tq[17],}\\\\\n"
"\\text{aq[5]} & \\rightarrow \\text{tq[25]}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\text{aq[0]} & \\rightarrow \\text{tq[15],}\\\\\n"
"\\text{aq[1]} & \\rightarrow \\text{tq[16],}\\\\\n"
"\\text{aq[2]} & \\rightarrow \\text{tq[19],}\\\\\n"
"\\text{aq[3]} & \\rightarrow \\text{tq[14],}\\\\\n"
"\\text{aq[4]} & \\rightarrow \\text{tq[17],}\\\\\n"
"\\text{aq[5]} & \\rightarrow \\text{tq[25]}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(b) This layout is not unique. Many other layouts avoid SWAP gates altogether. Another example is:\n"
msgstr "(b) Este layout no es único. Muchos otros layouts evitan por completo las puertas SWAP. Otro ejemplo es:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\text{aq[0]} & \\rightarrow \\text{tq[3],}\\\\\n"
"\\text{aq[1]} & \\rightarrow \\text{tq[4],}\\\\\n"
"\\text{aq[2]} & \\rightarrow \\text{tq[8],}\\\\\n"
"\\text{aq[3]} & \\rightarrow \\text{tq[2],}\\\\\n"
"\\text{aq[4]} & \\rightarrow \\text{tq[5],}\\\\\n"
"\\text{aq[5]} & \\rightarrow \\text{tq[13]}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\text{aq[0]} & \\rightarrow \\text{tq[3],}\\\\\n"
"\\text{aq[1]} & \\rightarrow \\text{tq[4],}\\\\\n"
"\\text{aq[2]} & \\rightarrow \\text{tq[8],}\\\\\n"
"\\text{aq[3]} & \\rightarrow \\text{tq[2],}\\\\\n"
"\\text{aq[4]} & \\rightarrow \\text{tq[5],}\\\\\n"
"\\text{aq[5]} & \\rightarrow \\text{tq[13]}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(c) Sometimes a specific qubit is more error-prone than most others on the chip. Also, some connections between qubits are more error-prone than others. The transpiler attempts to find a layout that avoids unnecessary SWAP gates, but that also uses the highest-fidelity qubits and connections available on the selected quantum computer.\n"
msgstr "(c) A veces un qubit específico es más propenso a errores que la mayoría de los demás del chip. Además, algunas conexiones entre qubits son más propensas a errores que otras. El transpilador intenta encontrar un layout que evite puertas SWAP innecesarias, pero que también use los qubits y las conexiones de mayor fidelidad disponibles en la computadora cuántica seleccionada.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reduce the effects of noise and errors {#reduce-the-effects-of-noise-and-errors}"
msgstr "Reducir los efectos del ruido y los errores {#reduce-the-effects-of-noise-and-errors}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Several Qiskit addons focus specifically on reducing the impact of noise and hardware imperfections.\n"
msgstr "Varios addons de Qiskit se centran específicamente en reducir el impacto del ruido y de las imperfecciones del hardware.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Operator backpropagation and noise-aware circuit transformations {#operator-backpropagation-and-noise-aware-circuit-transformations}"
msgstr "Retropropagación de operadores y transformaciones de circuitos conscientes del ruido {#operator-backpropagation-and-noise-aware-circuit-transformations}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We have already discussed operator propagation in the context of coherent Pauli checks in error correction. However, operator propagation is useful more generally. There are two main ways to use the propagation of an operator through a quantum circuit: (1) absorb the last few layers of a quantum circuit into the observables being measured, and (2) take into account the likely effects of errors in the circuit, and compensate for them by measuring a different observable. The next two tools use these approaches.\n"
msgstr "Ya hemos tratado la propagación de operadores en el contexto de las comprobaciones de Pauli coherentes en la corrección de errores. Sin embargo, la propagación de operadores es útil de forma más general. Hay dos formas principales de usar la propagación de un operador a través de un circuito cuántico: (1) absorber las últimas capas de un circuito cuántico en los observables que se miden, y (2) tener en cuenta los efectos probables de los errores en el circuito y compensarlos midiendo un observable diferente. Las siguientes dos herramientas usan estos enfoques.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Operator backpropagation {#operator-backpropagation}"
msgstr "Retropropagación de operadores {#operator-backpropagation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Operator backpropagation](/addons/qiskit-addon-obp) reduces circuit depth by absorbing gates from the end of a circuit into the measured observable. For example, consider the following circuit.\n"
msgstr "[La retropropagación de operadores](/addons/qiskit-addon-obp) reduce la profundidad del circuito absorbiendo puertas del final de un circuito en el observable medido. Por ejemplo, considera el siguiente circuito.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![An image showing a quantum circuit with several entangling and rotation layers, followed by a ladder of CNOTs from qubit 0 down to qubit 5. Finally, a Z measurement is made on qubit 5.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/backprop.avif)\n"
msgstr "![An image showing a quantum circuit with several entangling and rotation layers, followed by a ladder of CNOTs from qubit 0 down to qubit 5. Finally, a Z measurement is made on qubit 5.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/backprop.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This circuit contains rotation and entangling layers that appear nontrivial, followed by a ladder of CNOT gates and a measurement of `Z` on qubit 5. This circuit has a two-qubit depth of 7. This depth is before transpilation. In practice, you typically apply backpropagation after transpilation, but this example is for teaching purposes only. Recall that there are rules for propagating an observable past a gate. In particular, when a CNOT gate has target $q_t$ and control $q_c$, a $Z_t$ observable on $q_t$ becomes $Z_c Z_t$ when propagated backward past the CNOT gate: $Z_t \\rightarrow Z_c Z_t$. In this example circuit, if you propagate the observable $Z_5$ back through the entire ladder of CNOT gates, you get the observable $Z_5 Z_4 Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0$, or in standard Qiskit notation, simply $ZZZZZZ$. If we measure this observable instead of only $Z_5$, we can remove the entire ladder of CNOT gates, which reduces the two-qubit depth from 7 to 2. This observable still requires a measurement in only one basis on each qubit, so it does not increase the number of shots that we require. This is not always the case. Generally, more complicated observables require more shots, and sometimes more measurements in different bases.\n"
msgstr "Este circuito contiene capas de rotación y de entrelazamiento que parecen no triviales, seguidas de una escalera de puertas CNOT y una medición de `Z` en el qubit 5. Este circuito tiene una profundidad de dos qubits de 7. Esta profundidad es previa a la transpilación. En la práctica, normalmente se aplica la retropropagación después de la transpilación, pero este ejemplo es solo con fines didácticos. Recuerda que existen reglas para propagar un observable más allá de una puerta. En particular, cuando una puerta CNOT tiene objetivo $q_t$ y control $q_c$, un observable $Z_t$ sobre $q_t$ se convierte en $Z_c Z_t$ al propagarse hacia atrás más allá de la puerta CNOT: $Z_t \\rightarrow Z_c Z_t$. En este circuito de ejemplo, si propagas el observable $Z_5$ hacia atrás a través de toda la escalera de puertas CNOT, obtienes el observable $Z_5 Z_4 Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0$, o en la notación estándar de Qiskit, simplemente $ZZZZZZ$. Si medimos este observable en lugar de solo $Z_5$, podemos eliminar toda la escalera de puertas CNOT, lo que reduce la profundidad de dos qubits de 7 a 2. Este observable sigue requiriendo una medición en una sola base en cada qubit, por lo que no aumenta el número de shots que necesitamos. Esto no siempre es así. En general, los observables más complicados requieren más shots y, a veces, más mediciones en bases diferentes.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The overall strategy of operator backpropagation includes the following steps:\n"
msgstr "La estrategia general de la retropropagación de operadores incluye los siguientes pasos:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shorten the executed circuit\n"
msgstr "Acortar el circuito ejecutado\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Replace the original observable with an expanded observable\n"
msgstr "Reemplazar el observable original por un observable ampliado\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Trade circuit depth for increased sampling requirements\n"
msgstr "Intercambiar profundidad del circuito por mayores requisitos de muestreo\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The previous circuit is an obvious example in which backpropagation is advantageous. In general, however, it is not easy to identify the circuits that benefit most from backpropagation. To decide when to use backpropagation, check how much depth you can remove from your circuit, and weigh that reduction against the increased sampling requirements.\n"
msgstr "El circuito anterior es un ejemplo evidente en el que la retropropagación resulta ventajosa. En general, sin embargo, no es fácil identificar los circuitos que más se benefician de la retropropagación. Para decidir cuándo usar la retropropagación, comprueba cuánta profundidad puedes eliminar de tu circuito y sopesa esa reducción frente a los mayores requisitos de muestreo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Propagated noise absorption (PNA) {#propagated-noise-absorption-pna}"
msgstr "Absorción de ruido propagado (PNA) {#propagated-noise-absorption-pna}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Propagated noise absorption](/addons/qiskit-addon-pna) is structurally similar to operator backpropagation. However, instead of propagating an operator back through the ideal gates in a circuit, PNA incorporates a learned noise model and propagates the effects of noise directly into the observable. PNA does the following:\n"
msgstr "[La absorción de ruido propagado](/addons/qiskit-addon-pna) es estructuralmente similar a la retropropagación de operadores. Sin embargo, en lugar de propagar un operador hacia atrás a través de las puertas ideales de un circuito, PNA incorpora un modelo de ruido aprendido y propaga los efectos del ruido directamente al observable. PNA hace lo siguiente:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Learns noise behavior from the hardware\n"
msgstr "Aprende el comportamiento del ruido a partir del hardware\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Propagates the noise model through the circuit\n"
msgstr "Propaga el modelo de ruido a través del circuito\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Produces a modified observable that compensates for gate noise\n"
msgstr "Produce un observable modificado que compensa el ruido de las puertas\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![An image showing the gate errors on many layers of a quantum circuit being propagated forward to the final observable measurement.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/pna.avif)\n"
msgstr "![An image showing the gate errors on many layers of a quantum circuit being propagated forward to the final observable measurement.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/pna.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When the modified observable is measured on noisy hardware, the resulting expectation values better approximate the ideal noiseless result. PNA has two types of overhead. First, you must learn the noise model, which requires running additional circuits. Second, PNA can produce more complicated observables, which can increase sampling requirements.\n"
msgstr "Cuando el observable modificado se mide en hardware ruidoso, los valores esperados resultantes aproximan mejor el resultado ideal sin ruido. PNA tiene dos tipos de sobrecarga. Primero, debes aprender el modelo de ruido, lo que requiere ejecutar circuitos adicionales. Segundo, PNA puede producir observables más complicados, lo que puede aumentar los requisitos de muestreo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Circuit cutting {#circuit-cutting}"
msgstr "Corte de circuitos {#circuit-cutting}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Circuit cutting](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-cutting) partitions a large circuit into smaller subcircuits that can run independently. You then make enough measurements to recombine the results. Circuit cutting does the following:\n"
msgstr "[El corte de circuitos](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-cutting) divide un circuito grande en subcircuitos más pequeños que pueden ejecutarse de forma independiente. Después realizas suficientes mediciones para recombinar los resultados. El corte de circuitos hace lo siguiente:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reduces hardware requirements\n"
msgstr "Reduce los requisitos de hardware\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Allows computations larger than available qubit counts (wider circuits)\n"
msgstr "Permite cómputos mayores que el número de qubits disponibles (circuitos más anchos)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Helps address depth and connectivity limitations (deeper circuits)\n"
msgstr "Ayuda a superar las limitaciones de profundidad y conectividad (circuitos más profundos)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reconstructs the original result through classical post-processing\n"
msgstr "Reconstruye el resultado original mediante posprocesamiento clásico\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![An image showing two circuits being cut, so that they can be run separately and recombined later in post-processing.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/cutting.avif)\n"
msgstr "![An image showing two circuits being cut, so that they can be run separately and recombined later in post-processing.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/cutting.avif)\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Samplomatic {#samplomatic}"
msgstr "Samplomatic {#samplomatic}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Many of the techniques in the previous sections complement other suppression and mitigation methods covered throughout this course, including:\n"
msgstr "Muchas de las técnicas de las secciones anteriores complementan otros métodos de supresión y mitigación tratados a lo largo de este curso, entre ellos:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dynamical decoupling\n"
msgstr "Desacoplamiento dinámico\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli twirling\n"
msgstr "Pauli twirling\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "M3\n"
msgstr "M3\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "TREX\n"
msgstr "TREX\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE)\n"
msgstr "Extrapolación a ruido cero (ZNE)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Probabilistic error cancellation (PEC)\n"
msgstr "Cancelación probabilística de errores (PEC)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In many workflows, you can apply different techniques to different regions of the same circuit. As we have seen, many of these techniques also come with quantum overhead. We therefore sometimes need fine, detailed control over noise learning, sampling, and the application of twirling sequences. These are some of the motivations behind Samplomatic.\n"
msgstr "En muchos workflows, puedes aplicar diferentes técnicas a distintas regiones del mismo circuito. Como hemos visto, muchas de estas técnicas también conllevan sobrecarga cuántica. Por lo tanto, a veces necesitamos un control fino y detallado sobre el aprendizaje de ruido, el muestreo y la aplicación de secuencias de twirling. Estas son algunas de las motivaciones detrás de Samplomatic.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Samplomatic](/addons/samplomatic) is an open-source library that enables customized sampling, randomization, and error-mitigation workflows.\n"
msgstr "[Samplomatic](/addons/samplomatic) es una biblioteca de código abierto que permite workflows personalizados de muestreo, aleatorización y mitigación de errores.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Its first task is to analyze a circuit and divide it into labeled regions, or boxes. These boxes serve two purposes:\n"
msgstr "Su primera tarea es analizar un circuito y dividirlo en regiones etiquetadas, o cajas. Estas cajas tienen dos propósitos:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "They visually partition the circuit.\n"
msgstr "Dividen visualmente el circuito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "They create indexed regions that can be configured independently.\n"
msgstr "Crean regiones indexadas que pueden configurarse de forma independiente.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Users can attach annotations that describe how each box should be treated during execution. Examples include:\n"
msgstr "Los usuarios pueden adjuntar anotaciones que describen cómo debe tratarse cada caja durante la ejecución. Algunos ejemplos son:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying Pauli twirling to all boxes\n"
msgstr "Aplicar Pauli twirling a todas las cajas\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying twirling only to selected boxes\n"
msgstr "Aplicar twirling solo a las cajas seleccionadas\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using different twirling groups in different regions\n"
msgstr "Usar diferentes grupos de twirling en distintas regiones\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Injecting learned noise into specific layers\n"
msgstr "Inyectar ruido aprendido en capas específicas\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Customizing mitigation strategies at a fine-grained level\n"
msgstr "Personalizar las estrategias de mitigación a un nivel detallado\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Samplomatic also identifies repeated boxed regions. Because identical layers typically exhibit similar noise characteristics, you only need to perform noise learning once for each unique layer.\n"
msgstr "Samplomatic también identifica regiones en cajas que se repiten. Como las capas idénticas suelen presentar características de ruido similares, solo necesitas realizar el aprendizaje de ruido una vez para cada capa única.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Samplomatic outputs {#samplomatic-outputs}"
msgstr "Salidas de Samplomatic {#samplomatic-outputs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Samplomatic produces two primary objects:\n"
msgstr "Samplomatic produce dos objetos principales:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Template circuit\n"
msgstr "Circuito plantilla\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Samplex\n"
msgstr "Samplex\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The template circuit is a boxed, transpiled, parameterized circuit that is ready for execution. The samplex contains all the information that is required to generate and process circuit variants. Samplex contents include:\n"
msgstr "El circuito plantilla es un circuito parametrizado, transpilado y organizado en cajas, listo para su ejecución. El samplex contiene toda la información necesaria para generar y procesar variantes del circuito. El contenido del samplex incluye:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Parameter values for parameterized circuits\n"
msgstr "Valores de parámetros para circuitos parametrizados\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Randomization selections\n"
msgstr "Selecciones de aleatorización\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sampling distributions\n"
msgstr "Distribuciones de muestreo\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Post-processing information\n"
msgstr "Información de posprocesamiento\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Additional execution metadata\n"
msgstr "Metadatos de ejecución adicionales\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Formally, a samplex is a probability distribution over the parameters of a template circuit, together with auxiliary information that is required for execution and post-processing. An important practical advantage is that both the template circuit and the samplex are created locally on the client side. As a result, you can inspect, validate, and debug them before you use any hardware resources.\n"
msgstr "Formalmente, un samplex es una distribución de probabilidad sobre los parámetros de un circuito plantilla, junto con información auxiliar necesaria para la ejecución y el posprocesamiento. Una importante ventaja práctica es que tanto el circuito plantilla como el samplex se crean localmente en el lado del cliente. Como resultado, puedes inspeccionarlos, validarlos y depurarlos antes de usar cualquier recurso de hardware.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Samplomatic has many benefits, including fine-grained control of adaptive shot allocation and randomization. It also has logistical benefits, such as structured post-processing workflows. One of the most important benefits is the reuse of learned noise information across identical layers, which can save a significant amount of quantum computing time during noise learning.\n"
msgstr "Samplomatic tiene muchos beneficios, entre ellos el control detallado de la asignación adaptativa de shots y de la aleatorización. También ofrece beneficios logísticos, como flujos de posprocesamiento estructurados. Uno de los beneficios más importantes es la reutilización de la información de ruido aprendida entre capas idénticas, lo que puede ahorrar una cantidad significativa de tiempo de computación cuántica durante el aprendizaje de ruido.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shaded lightcones {#shaded-lightcones}"
msgstr "Conos de luz sombreados {#shaded-lightcones}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before you decide where to apply expensive mitigation techniques, it is helpful to identify the regions of a circuit that matter most to the observable that is being measured. This need motivates the [shaded lightcones](/addons/qiskit-addon-slc) addon. The idea of a lightcone comes from relativity, in which causal relationships are constrained by the finite speed at which information can travel.\n"
msgstr "Antes de decidir dónde aplicar técnicas de mitigación costosas, resulta útil identificar las regiones de un circuito que más importan para el observable que se está midiendo. Esta necesidad motiva el addon de [conos de luz sombreados](/addons/qiskit-addon-slc). La idea de un cono de luz proviene de la relatividad, donde las relaciones causales están limitadas por la velocidad finita a la que puede viajar la información.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![An image of spacetime. Time runs from bottom to top, and space runs from side to side. Because no causation can move through space faster than the speed of light, the region of spacetime that an event can causally influence is limited to a conical region. This is an analogy for the spreading of errors in a quantum circuit.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/lightcone.avif)\n"
msgstr "![An image of spacetime. Time runs from bottom to top, and space runs from side to side. Because no causation can move through space faster than the speed of light, the region of spacetime that an event can causally influence is limited to a conical region. This is an analogy for the spreading of errors in a quantum circuit.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/lightcone.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A similar concept applies in quantum circuits.\n"
msgstr "Un concepto similar se aplica en los circuitos cuánticos.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Consider a large circuit in which only a low-weight observable is of interest. A low-weight observable acts nontrivially on only a few qubits. Low-weight observables are of interest for many reasons. For example, they can represent the following:\n"
msgstr "Considera un circuito grande en el que solo interesa un observable de bajo peso. Un observable de bajo peso actúa de forma no trivial en solo unos pocos qubits. Los observables de bajo peso son de interés por muchas razones. Por ejemplo, pueden representar lo siguiente:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Individual terms within a larger Hamiltonian\n"
msgstr "Términos individuales dentro de un Hamiltoniano más grande\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A localized interaction region\n"
msgstr "Una región de interacción localizada\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Information collected onto a small set of ancilla qubits\n"
msgstr "Información recopilada en un conjunto pequeño de qubits auxiliares\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Other observables that involve only a few qubits\n"
msgstr "Otros observables que involucran solo unos pocos qubits\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Not every error in the circuit can affect the measurement outcome. This is especially true of Pauli errors, or any error that can be modeled as a set of Pauli operations. For example, look at the following circuit:\n"
msgstr "No todos los errores del circuito pueden afectar el resultado de la medición. Esto es especialmente cierto para los errores de Pauli, o cualquier error que se pueda modelar como un conjunto de operaciones de Pauli. Por ejemplo, observa el siguiente circuito:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A quantum circuit with an error on qubit 0 just before measurement. A measurement is performed only on qubit 6, and there is no entangling gate between qubits 0 and 6 in the final layer.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/lightcone-a.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A quantum circuit with an error on qubit 0 just before measurement. A measurement is performed only on qubit 6, and there is no entangling gate between qubits 0 and 6 in the final layer.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/lightcone-a.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A Pauli error on qubit 0 in the final layer cannot influence the measurement on qubit 6, because there is no connecting gate that could propagate the error from qubit 0 to qubit 6. Note that this argument does not apply to certain non-unitary errors. For example, a T1-like transition to the ground state on qubit 0 collapses qubit 0 to a computational basis state. If qubits 0 and 6 were previously entangled (as they are in this circuit), the non-unitary error on qubit 0 can affect qubit 6. The following discussion focuses on errors that can be represented as Pauli operations, or as probabilistic mixtures of Pauli operations.\n"
msgstr "Un error de Pauli en el qubit 0 de la última capa no puede influir en la medición del qubit 6, porque no hay ninguna puerta de conexión que pueda propagar el error del qubit 0 al qubit 6. Ten en cuenta que este argumento no se aplica a ciertos errores no unitarios. Por ejemplo, una transición de tipo T1 al estado fundamental en el qubit 0 colapsa el qubit 0 a un estado de la base computacional. Si los qubits 0 y 6 estaban previamente entrelazados (como ocurre en este circuito), el error no unitario en el qubit 0 puede afectar al qubit 6. La siguiente discusión se centra en los errores que se pueden representar como operaciones de Pauli, o como mezclas probabilísticas de operaciones de Pauli.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the last layer, only a Pauli error on qubit 5 or qubit 6 can directly affect the measurement on qubit 6.\n"
msgstr "En la última capa, solo un error de Pauli en el qubit 5 o en el qubit 6 puede afectar directamente la medición del qubit 6.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the entangling layer before that one, qubits 5 and 6 are entangled with qubits 4 and 7, respectively. Therefore, in that entangling layer or just before it, a Pauli error on any of those four qubits can affect the later measurement. You can continue to trace backward through the circuit to find the subset of gates and qubits that are causally connected to the measurement. This causal set forms a cone-shaped region in space (qubits) and time (layers), which gives rise to the term lightcone. The exact shape of the region varies from circuit to circuit. Because this analysis depends on hardware connectivity and gate placement, it is most useful after transpilation, routing, and layout optimization.\n"
msgstr "En la capa de entrelazamiento anterior, los qubits 5 y 6 están entrelazados con los qubits 4 y 7, respectivamente. Por lo tanto, en esa capa de entrelazamiento o justo antes de ella, un error de Pauli en cualquiera de esos cuatro qubits puede afectar la medición posterior. Puedes seguir rastreando hacia atrás a través del circuito para encontrar el subconjunto de puertas y qubits que están conectados causalmente con la medición. Este conjunto causal forma una región en forma de cono en el espacio (qubits) y el tiempo (capas), lo que da origen al término cono de luz. La forma exacta de la región varía de un circuito a otro. Como este análisis depende de la conectividad del hardware y de la ubicación de las puertas, es más útil después de la transpilación, el enrutamiento y la optimización del layout.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Beyond causal connectivity {#beyond-causal-connectivity}"
msgstr "Más allá de la conectividad causal {#beyond-causal-connectivity}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shaded lightcones extend this idea by also considering which types of errors matter.\n"
msgstr "Los conos de luz sombreados amplían esta idea al considerar también qué tipos de errores importan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For example, note the following:\n"
msgstr "Por ejemplo, ten en cuenta lo siguiente:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A Z error immediately before a Z-basis measurement has no effect on the measurement outcome.\n"
msgstr "Un error Z inmediatamente antes de una medición en la base Z no tiene efecto en el resultado de la medición.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "An X error immediately before a Z-basis measurement can dramatically change the result.\n"
msgstr "Un error X inmediatamente antes de una medición en la base Z puede cambiar drásticamente el resultado.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Some error types therefore deserve more mitigation effort than others. This distinction can substantially reduce the overhead of techniques such as PEC. In practice, the addon generates separate sensitivity analyses for each of the following error types:\n"
msgstr "Por lo tanto, algunos tipos de error merecen más esfuerzo de mitigación que otros. Esta distinción puede reducir sustancialmente el sobrecosto de técnicas como PEC. En la práctica, el addon genera análisis de sensibilidad independientes para cada uno de los siguientes tipos de error:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "X errors\n"
msgstr "X errors\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Z errors\n"
msgstr "Z errors\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Y (or XZ up to a phase) errors\n"
msgstr "Errores Y (o XZ salvo una fase)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This error sensitivity generally looks different for each error type, because different causally connected errors have different impacts on the measurement. Note also that the sensitivity changes throughout the circuit. An X error immediately before measurement might be highly damaging, while an error that occurs many layers earlier might have a smaller effect after it propagates through a highly entangled state.\n"
msgstr "Esta sensibilidad a los errores generalmente se ve diferente para cada tipo de error, porque distintos errores conectados causalmente tienen impactos diferentes en la medición. Ten en cuenta también que la sensibilidad cambia a lo largo del circuito. Un error X inmediatamente antes de la medición puede ser muy dañino, mientras que un error que ocurre muchas capas antes puede tener un efecto menor después de propagarse a través de un estado altamente entrelazado.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Three images showing the same quantum circuit, but with (a) no error, (b) an error just before measurement, and (c) an error earlier in the circuit.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/sensitivity.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Three images showing the same quantum circuit, but with (a) no error, (b) an error just before measurement, and (c) an error earlier in the circuit.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/sensitivity.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shaded lightcones quantify this difference by assigning a sensitivity value to potential errors throughout the circuit.\n"
msgstr "Los conos de luz sombreados cuantifican esta diferencia asignando un valor de sensibilidad a los errores potenciales en todo el circuito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The resulting maps indicate the following:\n"
msgstr "Los mapas resultantes indican lo siguiente:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Where errors matter\n"
msgstr "Dónde importan los errores\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Which error types matter\n"
msgstr "Qué tipos de error importan\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "How strongly they influence the final observable\n"
msgstr "Con qué intensidad influyen en el observable final\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Three images showing heat maps of error sensitivity to three different error types: X, Y, and Z.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/slc-xyz.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Three images showing heat maps of error sensitivity to three different error types: X, Y, and Z.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/modern-workflows/slc-xyz.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shaded lightcones do not mitigate errors themselves, but they can help focus mitigation effort where it provides the greatest benefit.\n"
msgstr "Los conos de luz sombreados no mitigan los errores por sí mismos, pero pueden ayudar a concentrar el esfuerzo de mitigación donde ofrece el mayor beneficio.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Learn and inject noise {#learn-and-inject-noise}"
msgstr "Aprender e inyectar ruido {#learn-and-inject-noise}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "After a circuit has been constructed, optimized, and annotated, two complementary tasks remain: learning the noise, and using the noise model (for example, to inject noise or to propagate the effects of noise).\n"
msgstr "Una vez que un circuito ha sido construido, optimizado y anotado, quedan dos tareas complementarias: aprender el ruido y usar el modelo de ruido (por ejemplo, para inyectar ruido o para propagar los efectos del ruido).\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "NoiseLearnerV3 {#noiselearnerv3}"
msgstr "NoiseLearnerV3 {#noiselearnerv3}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "NoiseLearnerV3 is the current tool for noise learning. The previous NoiseLearner interface accepted entire circuits and produced Pauli-Lindblad noise models. NoiseLearnerV3 instead operates directly on boxed circuit instructions. In summary, NoiseLearnerV3 does the following:\n"
msgstr "NoiseLearnerV3 es la herramienta actual para el aprendizaje de ruido. La interfaz anterior, NoiseLearner, aceptaba circuitos completos y producía modelos de ruido de Pauli-Lindblad. NoiseLearnerV3, en cambio, opera directamente sobre instrucciones de circuito organizadas en cajas. En resumen, NoiseLearnerV3 hace lo siguiente:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Accepts collections of labeled circuit layers\n"
msgstr "Acepta colecciones de capas de circuito etiquetadas\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reuses information from repeated layers\n"
msgstr "Reutiliza la información de las capas repetidas\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Supports measurement-noise learning\n"
msgstr "Admite el aprendizaje del ruido de medición\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Supports post-processing of learned models\n"
msgstr "Admite el posprocesamiento de los modelos aprendidos\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Enables noise injection and scaling workflows\n"
msgstr "Permite flujos de trabajo de inyección y escalado de ruido\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This design aligns closely with the layer-oriented workflow of Samplomatic. In particular, NoiseLearnerV3 uses the following methods for each instruction set:\n"
msgstr "Este diseño se alinea estrechamente con el flujo de trabajo orientado a capas de Samplomatic. En particular, NoiseLearnerV3 usa los siguientes métodos para cada conjunto de instrucciones:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli-Lindblad learning for gate operations\n"
msgstr "Aprendizaje de Pauli-Lindblad para operaciones de puertas\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "TREX-based learning for measurements\n"
msgstr "Aprendizaje basado en TREX para mediciones\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can then use a learned noise model in many of the methods that we have already covered. For example, recall that zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) with gate folding can lead to intractably deep circuits. The alternative method for scaling noise in that case was to sample from a known noise model, which effectively increases the noise level, even by non-integer factors. This method, probabilistic error amplification (PEA), is a good example of how you can use a noise model to mitigate errors. A good noise model is also required for probabilistic error cancellation (PEC) and propagated noise absorption (PNA).\n"
msgstr "Luego puedes usar un modelo de ruido aprendido en muchos de los métodos que ya hemos cubierto. Por ejemplo, recuerda que la extrapolación a ruido cero (ZNE) con plegado de puertas puede dar lugar a circuitos intratablemente profundos. El método alternativo para escalar el ruido en ese caso era muestrear a partir de un modelo de ruido conocido, lo que aumenta efectivamente el nivel de ruido, incluso con factores no enteros. Este método, la amplificación probabilística de errores (PEA), es un buen ejemplo de cómo puedes usar un modelo de ruido para mitigar errores. También se requiere un buen modelo de ruido para la cancelación probabilística de errores (PEC) y la absorción de ruido propagado (PNA).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In short, with a high-quality noise model, noise becomes a programmable resource rather than only a source of error.\n"
msgstr "En resumen, con un modelo de ruido de alta calidad, el ruido se convierte en un recurso programable en lugar de ser solo una fuente de error.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shaded lightcones versus NoiseLearnerV3 {#shaded-lightcones-versus-noiselearnerv3}"
msgstr "Conos de luz sombreados frente a NoiseLearnerV3 {#shaded-lightcones-versus-noiselearnerv3}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "NoiseLearnerV3 and SLC are closely related, but they take distinct inputs and answer different questions. SLC determines where to focus mitigation effort. NoiseLearnerV3 characterizes the actual noise present in those regions. These processes also involve different kinds of overhead. The following table summarizes these differences.\n"
msgstr "NoiseLearnerV3 y SLC están estrechamente relacionados, pero toman entradas distintas y responden preguntas diferentes. SLC determina dónde concentrar el esfuerzo de mitigación. NoiseLearnerV3 caracteriza el ruido real presente en esas regiones. Estos procesos también implican diferentes tipos de sobrecosto. La siguiente tabla resume estas diferencias.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|   | Shaded lightcones | NoiseLearnerV3 |\n"
"|---|-------------------|----------------|\n"
"| Purpose | Identifies where mitigation matters | Learns how errors behave |\n"
"| Overhead | Primarily classical overhead | Requires hardware executions |\n"
"| Output | Produces sensitivity maps | Produces noise-channel descriptions |\n"
"| Input | Uses circuit structure and operator propagation | Uses circuit structure and experimental hardware data |\n"
msgstr ""
"|   | Conos de luz sombreados | NoiseLearnerV3 |\n"
"|---|-------------------|----------------|\n"
"| Propósito | Identifica dónde importa la mitigación | Aprende cómo se comportan los errores |\n"
"| Sobrecosto | Principalmente sobrecosto clásico | Requiere ejecuciones en hardware |\n"
"| Salida | Produce mapas de sensibilidad | Produce descripciones de canales de ruido |\n"
"| Entrada | Usa la estructura del circuito y la propagación de operadores | Usa la estructura del circuito y datos experimentales del hardware |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Executor and runtime execution {#executor-and-runtime-execution}"
msgstr "Ejecución con Executor y en tiempo de ejecución {#executor-and-runtime-execution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Executor performs the final execution step. It can operate on either of the following inputs:\n"
msgstr "Executor realiza el paso final de ejecución. Puede operar con cualquiera de las siguientes entradas:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A template circuit and samplex generated by Samplomatic\n"
msgstr "Un circuito plantilla y un samplex generados por Samplomatic\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A conventional quantum circuit without Samplomatic\n"
msgstr "Un circuito cuántico convencional sin Samplomatic\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With this flexibility, you can adopt as many or as few components of the directed execution workflow as you need.\n"
msgstr "Con esta flexibilidad, puedes adoptar tantos o tan pocos componentes del flujo de trabajo de ejecución dirigida como necesites.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
